.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt MOUNT 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount
.Nd list or add a file: mount
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Ar scheme: path
.Nm
.Fl -selftest
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no operands,
.Nm
reads the static mount table from
.Pa /etc/mounts
and prints one line per entry:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<scheme> on <path>
.Ed
.Pp
Protocol version 1 has no
.Dv LISTMOUNTS
control operation, so the static file is the source of the listing.
.Pp
With two operands,
.Nm
asks
.Xr vfsd 8
to mount
.Ar scheme:
.Pq a name ending in a colon
at the absolute
.Ar path .
The mount point does not have to exist in the underlying server; VFS merges
the mount into the namespace.
.Pp
.Fl -selftest
lists the static table, mounts
.Ql ramfs:
at
.Pa /mnt ,
unmounts it, and prints
.Dq mount: selftest ok .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2.
A rejected mount exits with status 1.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr umount 8 ,
.Xr vfsd 8 ,
.Xr scheme 7
.Sh STANDARDS
The mount table is a RavenBSD protocol-version-1 interface.
